                            <comment id="495220" author="adilger" created="Thu, 28 May 2026 20:56:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Still seeing this failing in sanity-compr test_1000.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495221" author="adilger" created="Thu, 28 May 2026 21:06:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzzz&quot;&gt;bzzz&lt;/a&gt; I was looking at the allocations for one of the test failures (&lt;tt&gt;review-dne-subtest-change&lt;/tt&gt;) which is being run in isolation:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/a82ba2c7-7cd6-43c6-af7e-09dee55969d1&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/a82ba2c7-7cd6-43c6-af7e-09dee55969d1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It appears that the &lt;tt&gt;dense=0&lt;/tt&gt; file &lt;em&gt;starts&lt;/em&gt; by allocating a bunch of blocks (60) contiguously, and then starts allocating them discontiguously (66), while the reverse is true for the &lt;tt&gt;dense=1&lt;/tt&gt; file (about 30 discont + 17 cont), so the test fails with &quot;&lt;tt&gt;dense (48) should have fewer extents (67)&lt;/tt&gt;&quot;.  In my test patch there are consistently &lt;em&gt;fewer&lt;/em&gt; fragments in the &lt;tt&gt;dense=1&lt;/tt&gt; case (around 40), while the &lt;tt&gt;dense=0&lt;/tt&gt; case varies between 80-120 so it isn&apos;t hitting the 3x ratio consistently, with a few just below 2x ratio.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I might be able to make the test pass more consistently by allocating more blocks to each file, but I&apos;m wondering if this is exposing some kind of bug in the mballoc code?  Is there some kind of &quot;allocation history&quot; or &quot;use up current allocations&quot; (either at the block or object level, for either the dense or sparse allocator) that needs to be done until the new setting takes effect?  This &lt;b&gt;should&lt;/b&gt; be handled immediately on a per-file basis depending on whether the client is sending compressed/sparse writes, but it seems like something is not quite right.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495260" author="bzzz" created="Sat, 30 May 2026 17:41:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;adilger&quot;&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt; there is a diff between exa6 and master branch:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
@@ -3718,6 +3730,7 @@ &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ldiskfs_mb_init(struct super_block *
 	sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_max_to_scan = MB_DEFAULT_MAX_TO_SCAN;
 	sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_min_to_scan = MB_DEFAULT_MIN_TO_SCAN;
 	sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_stats = MB_DEFAULT_STATS;
+	sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_stream_request = MB_DEFAULT_STREAM_THRESHOLD;
 	sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_order2_reqs = MB_DEFAULT_ORDER2_REQS;
 	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (!sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_c1_blocks)
 		sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_c1_blocks =
@@ -5543,8 +5566,8 @@ &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; void ldiskfs_mb_group_or_file(str
 		inode_pa_eligible = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;;
 
 	size = max(size, isize);
-	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; ((ac-&amp;gt;ac_o_ex.fe_len &amp;gt;= sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_small_req) ||
-	    (size &amp;gt;= sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_large_req))
+	&lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* Don&apos;t use group allocation &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; large files */&lt;/span&gt;
+	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (size &amp;gt; sbi-&amp;gt;s_mb_stream_request)
 		group_pa_eligible = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;;
 
 	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (!group_pa_eligible) {
--- ldiskfs/ldiskfs.h	2026-05-30 20:04:23.626242991 +0300
+++ ../head1/ldiskfs/ldiskfs.h	2026-05-30 20:34:01.380466202 +0300
@@ -1530,6 +1531,7 @@ struct ldiskfs_sb_info {
 	&lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* tunables */&lt;/span&gt;
 	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; s_stripe;
 	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; s_mb_max_linear_groups;
+	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; s_mb_stream_request;
 	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; s_mb_small_req;
 	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; s_mb_large_req;
 	unsigned &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; s_mb_max_to_scan;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;which explains why exa6 passes the test.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495402" author="adilger" created="Tue, 2 Jun 2026 20:55:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzzz&quot;&gt;bzzz&lt;/a&gt;, is this missing from some patch ported between the branches?  It looks like &lt;tt&gt;ext4-prealloc.patch&lt;/tt&gt; is explicitly removing the usage of &lt;tt&gt;s_mb_stream_request&lt;/tt&gt; and replacing them with &lt;tt&gt;s_mb_small_req&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;s_mb_large_req&lt;/tt&gt;, but maybe it is time to get rid of that patch?  I don&apos;t think we have every used that functionality.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="498628" author="adilger" created="Mon, 27 Jul 2026 21:03:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It appears that the &lt;tt&gt;ext4-mballoc-dense.patch&lt;/tt&gt; is missing from newer kernel series like el9, el10, ubuntu and the sanity-compr.sh test_1000 subtest is skipped in this case.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
